These are results for json-render if there are 3 elements in schema how do you render one of them\nSearch instead for ijson-render if there3 are 3 elements in schema how do you render one of them\nAI Overview\nTo render only one element from a json-render specification containing multiple elements, change the root property in your spec object to point exclusively to the ID of the target element you want to display, leaving the unselected elements out of the root's tree or children array. \nHow to Isolate a Single Element\nChange the root pointer: Set root to point directly to the key of the specific element you want to render.\nRemove child links: Ensure the targeted element does not include the other elements inside its children array.\nFilter the elements map: Pass only the required element (and any nested dependencies it needs) inside the elements dictionary. \nCode Example\njavascript\nconst spec = {\n  // Point the root directly to the one element you want to render\n  root: "element-2", \n  elements: {\n    "element-2": {\n      type: "Button",\n      props: { label: "Only Me" },\n      children: []\n    }\n    // element-1 and element-3 are omitted entirely from the spec tree\n  }\n};\n\n<Renderer spec={spec} registry={registry} />
