In json-render, delivery for rendering involves transmitting generative UI specifications from a backend model or data source to a client. The primary delivery formats include SpecStream (JSONL patch streaming via RFC 6902), Standalone Mode (full-page UI specs), and Inline Mode (mixed conversational text and UI patches).Delivery ModesStandalone Mode: The AI outputs a complete UI spec payload without conversational prose, ideal for dedicated dashboards, builders, and playgrounds.Inline Mode: The AI replies with conversational text while dynamically injecting UI specs inline, ideal for copilots and chatbots.Stream & Patch MechanicsSpecStream (JSONL): Streams data line by line where each line is an incremental JSON patch (add, replace, etc.) following RFC 6902.Progressive Client Hook: The client-side hook processes each incoming patch instantly to mount components piece-by-piece without layout spinners.Output Targets & RenderersWeb Frameworks: Maps specs to React, Vue, Svelte, Solid, or shadcn/ui components.Mobile & Specialized Formats: Renders natively via React Native, generates timelines with Remotion, or outputs document structures using React PDF.If you'd like, let me know:Your chosen frontend framework (React, Vue, etc.)Your delivery target (web, mobile, or video/PDF export)I can provide code snippets or architecture patterns for your setup.GitHubREADME.md - vercel-labs/json-render - GitHubTable_title: Packages Table_content: | Package | Description | | --- | --- | | @json-render/react-native | React Native renderer w...
