it. * SpecStream Format# json-render uses SpecStream, a JSONL-based streaming format where...Show allwhat are the arguments to pas s for antigravity chat interfaceIn the context of programmatically orchestrating or interacting with Google's Antigravity CLI or the underlying Antigravity SDK, managing the built-in chat session requires passing specific orchestrated fields.Because the runtime manages multi-turn agentic workflows dynamically, the configuration relies on core structured variables passed down to standard input or the session manager.Programmatic Session Arguments (antigravity.chat)When interacting with the built-in chat orchestration commands natively or via extension APIs, you pass three core payload parameters:sessionId: A unique string ID to target, resume, or fork a specific active chat context. If passed as null, it spins up a completely new conversation.payload: The primary wrapper object containing the message payload.context: An attached metadata object used to automatically supply the chat with active code selections, workspace file paths, and environment logs.CLI Execution & Daemon ArgumentsWhen launching or bridging the Antigravity chat interface from a developer terminal or a quick action workflow, the following flags control the instance session:--model: Declares a specific LLM to govern the chat session (e.g., --model="Gemini 3.5 Flash (High)" or --model="Claude Sonnet 4.6 (Thinking)").--remote-debugging-port: Exposes Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP) ports (typically 9000) so external scripts can listen to conversational DOM states.Hook Payload Structural Arguments (hooks.json)If you are passing arguments down to custom lifecycle interceptors (such as checking tools before the chat agent executes code), the Go-based agy runtime pipes arguments through standard input (stdin). The data fields must match this structure under .toolCall.args:CommandLine: The exact shell instructions proposed by the chat agent.Cwd: The absolute current working directory of the project scope.WaitMsBeforeAsync: The execution polling delay in milliseconds.If you are trying to hook up Vercel's json-render natively to receive the structural outputs from an Antigravity agent, you will want to listen to the response.tool_calls stream payload directly.If you'd like, let me know:If you are invoking this inside a VS Code extension wrapper or from a raw terminal script.Whether you want to enforce specific Zod schema boundaries on the generated chat artifacts.I can provide a concrete configuration snippet or an API structure.
