To build a group chat interface using JSONL patch rendering, you need a structured catalog of chat components. Below is the blueprint for a standard group chat UI that can be streamed and rendered inline.📋 Component Schema CatalogThis schema defines the allowed building blocks your AI can stream to render the group chat.json{\n  "$schema": "https://json-render.dev",\n  "name": "group-chat-bundle",\n  "components": [\n    {\n      "name": "ChatHeader",\n      "properties": {\n        "title": { "type": "string" },\n        "memberCount": { "type": "integer" },\n        "avatars": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "ChatMessage",\n      "properties": {\n        "id": { "type": "string" },\n        "senderName": { "type": "string" },\n        "avatarUrl": { "type": "string" },\n        "text": { "type": "string" },\n        "timestamp": { "type": "string" },\n        "isCurrentUser": { "type": "boolean" }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "ActiveTyping",\n      "properties": {\n        "users": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } }\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\nUse code with caution.⚡ Inline JSON Stream ExampleThis is the standard JSONL payload format the model emits inside the chat window to dynamically render the UI.jsonl{"op": "add", "path": "/header", "value": {"component": "ChatHeader", "props": {"title": "Dev Team Sync", "memberCount": 4, "avatars": ["https://pravatar.cc", "https://pravatar.cc", "https://pravatar.cc"]}}}\n{"op": "add", "path": "/messages/-", "value": {"component": "ChatMessage", "props": {"id": "msg_001", "senderName": "Sarah", "avatarUrl": "https://pravatar.cc", "text": "Did anyone review the new UI schemas?", "timestamp": "08:45 AM", "isCurrentUser": false}}}\n{"op": "add", "path": "/messages/-", "value": {"component": "ChatMessage", "props": {"id": "msg_002", "senderName": "Alex", "avatarUrl": "https://pravatar.cc", "text": "Just looking at them now. Looks clean!", "timestamp": "08:46 AM", "isCurrentUser": true}}}\n{"op": "set", "path": "/typing", "value": {"component": "ActiveTyping", "props": {"users": ["Elena"]}}}\nUse code with caution.🛠️ Frontend Implementation (React Example)This maps incoming components from the registry to your actual application widgets safely.tsximport { Registry } from '@json-render/react';\n\nconst chatRegistry = new Registry();\n\nchatRegistry.register('ChatHeader', ({ title, memberCount }) => (\n  <div className="flex justify-between p-4 border-b bg-gray-50">\n    <h3 className="font-bold">{title}</h3>\n    <span className="text-sm text-gray-500">{memberCount} participants</span>\n  </div>\n));\n\nchatRegistry.register('ChatMessage', ({ senderName, text, timestamp, isCurrentUser }) => (\n  <div className={`flex flex-col my-2 p-3 rounded-lg max-w-xs ${isCurrentUser ? 'bg-blue-500 text-white ml-auto' : 'bg-gray-200 mr-auto'}`}>\n    <span className="text-xs font-semibold opacity-75">{senderName}</span>\n    <p className="text-sm">{text}</p>\n    <span className="text-[10px] opacity-50 text-right mt-1">{timestamp}</span>\n  </div>\n));\nUse code with caution.If you are building this out, tell me:Do you need to include rich media support (images, code snippets, attachments)?Should we design custom interactive widgets like group polls or event RSVPs?I can expand the schema files and payload rules for those specific interactions.
